{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "harnessVersion": "0.4.0",
  "description": "Record of the file set bin/sh-install.sh stages into a target. The installer does not read this file; tests/install-manifest-contract.sh proves a real install produces exactly this set, byte for byte.",
  "substitutions": {
    "placeholder": "{name}",
    "projectName": {
      "default": "basename of the resolved target directory when no name is passed",
      "mustBeNonEmpty": true,
      "forbiddenCharacters": [
        "LF",
        "CR",
        "TAB",
        "/",
        "\\"
      ],
      "note": "The installer refuses a name containing any forbidden character (exit 2). Every other character, including $, &, backticks and {{...}}, is taken literally."
    },
    "tokens": {
      "{{PROJECT_NAME}}": "{name}",
      "{{DIR}}": "{name} (repo root - base rules)"
    },
    "rule": "Only the tokens listed in an entry's own tokens array are replaced in that entry; every other {{...}} token in the source survives untouched. Replacement is literal (no escape or back-reference processing), single pass, every occurrence on each line. A substituted value is never rescanned. {name} in a token value is the project name."
  },
  "directories": [
    ".claude/agents",
    ".claude/commands",
    ".claude/commands/spec-harness",
    ".claude/skills",
    ".claude/spec-harness/methods",
    ".agents/skills",
    ".agents/skills/sdd",
    ".memory",
    "ai_rules/rules",
    "learning",
    "learning/lessons",
    "specs",
    "workflows"
  ],
  "installRecord": {
    "record": ".spec-harness/install.json",
    "baseDir": ".spec-harness/base",
    "note": "The installer also writes this record of what it staged (format spec-harness-install-record) and one base copy of every file it added, under baseDir at the same relative path. status, update and uninstall read them. A file that already existed and differs from the harness file is recorded as not managed and has no base copy. A file that already existed and is byte-identical to the harness file is recorded as managed and gets a base copy."
  },
  "loaderBlock": "## Spec Harness\n\n- Setup status: `SPEC-HARNESS.md`. Keep PENDING items PENDING until they are checked.\n- Before code edits read `ai_rules/rules/frequent_rules.md`, `.memory/40-active.md` and the nearest `RULES.md`.\n- Feature work goes through `/sdd <ticket text>`. The procedure is `.claude/commands/sdd.md`.\n- A code ticket is any change to a tracked file outside `specs/` and `.memory/`. It goes through `/sdd` before the first source edit, even when it looks small: the light route is still `/sdd`. Keep the ticket's code inside this repository: no worktree, clone or copy elsewhere unless the user asks for one.\n- A task is done when a fresh verifier returns PASS against the ticket's own goal, not when tests pass.\n- Rules change only through `.claude/commands/spec-harness/learn.md`, after review.\n",
